  "findings": [
    "Both learned point arms retain exactly the same legal point domains, legal candidate incidence, generations, every decision/placement/restore sequence, full saved solutions and all per-query counters as their no-learning point arms. This is stronger than aggregate equality.",
    "The full graph records are not byte-identical: static dependency tables add learned guard R_4 to point (26,8) and R_5 to (32,8); a few intermediate states additionally carry assigned zero. These structural/mark differences do not change the observed legal domains or scheduler choices.",
    "Every learned-guard activation occurs after all four original guards and after an existing variable assignment already satisfies the learned clause. B07 has all four variable and original tuple carriers saturated first. B08 has ten earlier activations per guard relative to full saturation, but all clauses are already satisfied. Six R_5 activations precede their own tuple carrier, whose two legal candidates already both carry zero.",
    "Ordinary assignments fall from72 to64 (B07) and80 to74 (B08); B08 unit decisions fall68 to62 while branches stay12. Literal checks increase960 to1344 and1152 to1586. Representation-specific counts are not directly comparable work units.",
    "One noisy suite does not establish speedup. Inclusive first-use costs must include the recorded shared discovery/certification cost once for each learned strategy considered separately; they must not sum nested clocks or duplicate that cost in the physical suite total.",
    "All proposals come from complete failed root queries and negate the whole boundary; first-two distinct non-original selection and all48 queries per case are preserved. Entailment/preservation is cross-checked against the saved accepted sets, not a recomputed truth oracle."
